WEBVTT

00:00:00.596 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.713 --> 00:00:06.350
In this lesson, we do a classic French, then an ombré, step by step.

00:00:06.936 --> 00:00:11.576
Nail prep, the base coat and curing are exactly as in the gel polish lesson,

00:00:11.526 --> 00:00:13.630
so I will only recap them briefly.

00:00:14.116 --> 00:00:17.230
Our time goes to the smile line, and to blending the color.

00:00:17.887 --> 00:00:18.689
Step one:

00:00:18.876 --> 00:00:19.889
prep the nails.

00:00:20.126 --> 00:00:21.833
Wash and sanitize your hands,

00:00:21.783 --> 00:00:25.089
and look closely at the nails and the skin of the client.

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:27.089
Dry prep, no soaking.

00:00:27.598 --> 00:00:31.690
Push back the cuticle, remove the thin layer of skin on the nail plate,

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:33.569
buff lightly to remove the shine,

00:00:33.853 --> 00:00:35.009
then wipe off the oil.

00:00:35.439 --> 00:00:39.329
Finish the nail shape first, because the smile line has to suit the shape.

00:00:39.678 --> 00:00:41.649
Only once the shape is done do you paint.

00:00:42.318 --> 00:00:43.173
Step two:

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:45.253
base coat, then the pink base.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:50.292
A thin base coat, capping the free edge, cured for the time the brand gives.

00:00:50.697 --> 00:00:54.853
Then one or two coats of sheer pink, thin, each cured separately.

00:00:55.282 --> 00:00:59.013
A slightly more opaque base helps to hide a crooked natural free edge.

00:00:59.701 --> 00:01:00.551
Step three:

00:01:00.884 --> 00:01:02.231
choose the smile line.

00:01:02.718 --> 00:01:04.951
Look at all ten nails before you paint.

00:01:05.376 --> 00:01:07.811
Choose the depth based on the shortest nail,

00:01:07.761 --> 00:01:10.631
or the nail with the most crooked natural free edge,

00:01:10.741 --> 00:01:12.471
so the whole set can be made even.

00:01:13.061 --> 00:01:14.631
Picture the points beforehand:

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:19.013
a point at each corner of the tip, at the same depth, and a point in the middle,

00:01:18.963 --> 00:01:20.791
where the smile line is shallowest.

00:01:21.359 --> 00:01:22.238
Step four:

00:01:22.533 --> 00:01:23.438
paint the white.

00:01:24.233 --> 00:01:28.318
Take a little white gel on the liner brush, just enough, not too much.

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:32.718
Place the brush at a corner of the tip, exactly on the point you chose.

00:01:33.216 --> 00:01:36.638
Then pull the brush along the curve, to the middle point of the nail.

00:01:37.146 --> 00:01:38.318
Keep your hand steady.

00:01:38.907 --> 00:01:41.820
Turn the finger of the client gently with the brush stroke,

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:43.518
rather than turning your own wrist.

00:01:43.769 --> 00:01:48.039
On the little finger, the nail is small, so the white shrinks with it,

00:01:47.989 --> 00:01:52.078
but to the eye, the depth must look the same as on the other nails.

00:01:52.727 --> 00:01:55.137
Then do exactly the same from the other corner.

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:59.822
Place the brush at the opposite corner, exactly as deep as the first corner,

00:01:59.772 --> 00:02:01.297
then pull it to the middle,

00:02:01.413 --> 00:02:04.497
so the two halves meet in a single continuous curve.

00:02:04.922 --> 00:02:08.897
Fill in the white out to the edge, and sweep lightly over the edge of the tip.

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:10.897
The white layer must be thin.

00:02:11.309 --> 00:02:14.337
If it is not white enough yet, leave that for the next layer.

00:02:14.961 --> 00:02:15.853
Step five:

00:02:16.113 --> 00:02:18.093
clean the smile line before curing.

00:02:18.491 --> 00:02:21.264
Take a small flat brush, dip it in cleanser,

00:02:21.214 --> 00:02:24.173
then blot it on a towel until it is almost dry,

00:02:24.282 --> 00:02:25.453
only slightly damp.

00:02:26.024 --> 00:02:28.844
Glide the brush along the inner edge of the white,

00:02:28.794 --> 00:02:30.893
to cut the smile line crisp and even.

00:02:31.307 --> 00:02:34.413
If the brush is too wet, the cleanser will make the white bleed.

00:02:34.833 --> 00:02:36.573
Wipe the brush after every stroke.

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:38.569
And if you paint it crooked?

00:02:39.268 --> 00:02:42.089
Before curing, it is very easy to fix:

00:02:42.439 --> 00:02:46.489
take a brush with cleanser, wipe the white off that nail, and paint it again.

00:02:47.078 --> 00:02:50.169
Never cure a crooked nail, intending to fix it later.

00:02:50.827 --> 00:02:55.129
Cured gel has to be buffed off, which wastes time and thins the base.

00:02:55.565 --> 00:02:56.329
Another trick:

00:02:56.752 --> 00:03:00.889
paint a few nails, then cure, rather than painting the whole hand at once.

00:03:01.068 --> 00:03:04.381
And keep the hand of the client away from the lamp while you paint,

00:03:04.331 --> 00:03:08.569
because stray light can make the gel start to set before you have cleaned up the line.

00:03:09.231 --> 00:03:10.095
Step six:

00:03:10.338 --> 00:03:11.535
cure for the full time.

00:03:11.708 --> 00:03:15.116
If you need it whiter, add one more layer, thin as well,

00:03:15.066 --> 00:03:18.175
following exactly the same line, clean up the line,

00:03:18.252 --> 00:03:19.135
then cure again.

00:03:19.649 --> 00:03:23.535
Two thin layers always look better and last longer than one thick layer.

00:03:24.199 --> 00:03:25.069
Step seven:

00:03:25.249 --> 00:03:26.029
the top coat.

00:03:26.515 --> 00:03:30.589
Cover the whole nail, sweep over the edge of the tip, and cure for the full time.

00:03:31.071 --> 00:03:33.789
If the top coat leaves a sticky layer, wipe it off.

00:03:34.298 --> 00:03:36.029
Then comes the most important part:

00:03:36.298 --> 00:03:38.029
checking all ten nails.

00:03:38.378 --> 00:03:41.629
Ask the client to lay her hands flat, and look from above.

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:43.069
Is the depth the same?

00:03:43.372 --> 00:03:44.669
Are both corners balanced?

00:03:45.177 --> 00:03:48.509
If a nail is off, fix it now, before the client leaves.

00:03:49.064 --> 00:03:50.530
Now, the ombré.

00:03:50.927 --> 00:03:53.250
Prep and base coat exactly as above.

00:03:53.678 --> 00:03:57.330
Then a very thin layer of pink, or nude, cured.

00:03:57.876 --> 00:03:59.802
This base is the color at the cuticle,

00:03:59.752 --> 00:04:02.370
so choose a shade that suits the skin of the client.

00:04:02.796 --> 00:04:06.692
For the white, many technicians choose a slightly sheer milky white,

00:04:06.642 --> 00:04:08.050
rather than solid white,

00:04:08.242 --> 00:04:10.690
because it is softer, and easier to blend.

00:04:11.331 --> 00:04:12.126
Step two:

00:04:12.387 --> 00:04:16.046
apply the white, only on the tip, about the front third of the nail.

00:04:16.395 --> 00:04:17.406
A thin layer;

00:04:17.672 --> 00:04:19.246
it does not need to look good yet.

00:04:19.596 --> 00:04:22.915
Do not bring the white up near the cuticle, because when you blend,

00:04:22.865 --> 00:04:24.526
the color will travel further up.

00:04:25.193 --> 00:04:26.056
Step three:

00:04:26.238 --> 00:04:27.256
blend the color.

00:04:27.576 --> 00:04:28.536
The first way:

00:04:28.725 --> 00:04:31.416
use a clean flat brush, almost dry.

00:04:31.925 --> 00:04:35.891
Place the brush where the white meets the pink, and pull very short,

00:04:35.841 --> 00:04:38.136
very light strokes towards the cuticle.

00:04:38.441 --> 00:04:39.656
Wipe the brush often.

00:04:40.162 --> 00:04:41.096
The second way:

00:04:41.284 --> 00:04:45.985
use a small sponge, and dab lightly over the color change, many times,

00:04:45.935 --> 00:04:48.376
so the white fades gradually upward.

00:04:48.872 --> 00:04:52.056
The sponge is used for a single client, then thrown away.

00:04:52.299 --> 00:04:57.035
Whichever way you use, do one nail at a time, and cure right after blending,

00:04:56.985 --> 00:05:00.056
so the color has no time to run back into a band.

00:05:00.737 --> 00:05:01.589
Step four:

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:03.349
cure, then look again.

00:05:03.754 --> 00:05:05.429
Is the color change soft yet?

00:05:05.607 --> 00:05:06.869
Is the tip white enough?

00:05:07.186 --> 00:05:09.493
If not, add another layer, thin as well,

00:05:09.443 --> 00:05:12.709
placing the white a little lower than the previous layer,

00:05:12.854 --> 00:05:14.229
blend, then cure.

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:17.189
Usually two to three thin layers look beautiful.

00:05:17.537 --> 00:05:21.909
A band or streaks are a sign that a layer was too thick, or not blended enough.

00:05:22.542 --> 00:05:23.353
Last step:

00:05:23.542 --> 00:05:28.313
the top coat, cured for the full time, then a drop of cuticle oil around the nails.

00:05:28.624 --> 00:05:30.233
Check all ten nails again:

00:05:30.502 --> 00:05:32.793
the color fade must look the same on each.

00:05:33.178 --> 00:05:38.633
Once the client has gone, used sponges, cotton and files go in a bin with a lid.

00:05:39.011 --> 00:05:41.513
Metal tools go to be cleaned and sterilized.

00:05:41.791 --> 00:05:44.793
Wipe the brushes, and close the gel bottles tightly.

00:05:45.142 --> 00:05:47.753
And now, take the short quiz below the video.
